{{--
    Fable: the icon pattern. Draws the value of the CSS variable --fable-pattern: one small seamless tile, a 7 by 7
    grid of single-colour icons, as an inline data-URI SVG made here (nothing is fetched from outside). The pages put
    the value on a solid area carrying the `.patterned` class (see fable-home.css), which lays the tile over the
    area's own colour. Draws nothing when the pattern is off, so the area stays solid.

    Takes (all optional):
      $pattern    none (off), sections, pets, home or food: the set of seven icons the tile is made of
      $strength   subtle, medium or bold: how visible the icons are
      $density    sparse, regular or dense: how close together they sit
      $accent     a #rrggbb colour: one icon in seven takes it (white and accent); empty keeps every icon white

    The icons are Phosphor (regular weight, MIT licence), one path each on a 256 by 256 grid. To use your own, put
    the path data of any single-colour SVG icon in $icons and name it in a set.

    @package egberipiribo
    @since   0.1.0
--}}
